20 0 obj
<< /A 282 0 R /Alt (Two Kaplan-Meier survival plots display overall survival on the left and progression-free survival on the right for patients after HSCT, categorized by disease status: active disease, complete remission greater than one \(CR>1\), and first complete remission \(CR1\). Survival probabilities are highest for CR1, intermediate for CR>1, and lowest for active disease over five years. Number at risk tables for each group are shown below each plot for specific time points.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 15 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 283 0 R /Alt (Two Kaplan-Meier survival curves at 2 years landmark analysis compare outcomes for hematopoietic stem cell transplant patients by disease status at transplant: active disease \(black\), complete remission greater than one \(CR>1, red\), and first complete remission \(CR1, green\). The left panel shows overall survival, with CR1 group having the highest survival, while CR>1 and active disease show superimposable outcome. The right panel displays progression-free survival, again with the CR1 group performing best. Tables below each graph provide the number at risk at sequential years post-transplant.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 16 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
